config ALLOW_UNINTEGRATED
    bool "Allow Unintegrated Options"
    default n
    option no_fuzz
    help
      It's been a long time of trying to get integration to work with all 3 architectures,
      and at times it seems like one step forward, three steps back, so I'm putting down
      the heavy hammer and marking most "extra" kernel options with this flag,
      so that I can figure out a minimal kernel which can work for all 3.
      This also gives me a way to signal which options/drivers/subsystems have actually
      been tested along the way (and *should* be okay to enable in a version which students
      get to use in a class like 343 or 446)

# --- Invisible Options ---

# Features

config HAS_PORT_IO
    def_bool n
    help
      Does the current configuration have support for Port Mapped I/O?

config HAS_PCI
    def_bool n
    help
      Does the current configuration have support for PCI devices?

config HAS_MSI
    def_bool n
    help
      Does the current configuration have support for MSI interrupts? (set by the architecture or irq device)

# Multi Processing

# FDT
config USE_FDT
    def_bool n
    help
      Use the Open Firmware device tree to discover devices.

# Multiboot
config USE_MULTIBOOT
    def_bool n
    help
      Use Mutliboot when booting the system

# PCI
config USE_PCI_CAM
    def_bool n
    depends on HAS_PORT_IO
    help
      Use the Port Mapped I/O to access PCI configuration space

config USE_PCI_ECAM
    def_bool n
    help
      Use the MMIO "Enhanced Configuration Access Mechanism" to access PCI configuration space

# IRQ
config IDENTITY_MAP_IRQ_VECTORS
    def_bool n
    help
      Identity map IRQ's to Vectors for architectures where there isn't a conceptual difference between the two.

config SPARSE_IRQ
    def_bool n
    help
      Store Interrupt Vectors's efficiently on a system where there can be large gaps between IRQ numbers.
      If this is disabled, the architecture will need to provide the MAX_IRQ_NUM macro.

config CONFIG
    def_bool y
    help
      This should remain hidden, it can be used to check whether or not the configuration
      has been loaded correctly and should always be defined and evaluate to "y"

